  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lynyrd Skynyrd's greatest hits feels like a natural next choice because I have repeatedly chosen hits collections and classic rock compilations.",
    "Led Zeppelin IV connects with my listening to The Cars and older rock, so an individual album can appeal even when I often choose compilations."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Miss Thang does not give me the same connection to the older rock and familiar-song collections I want today.",
    "West Side Story is less appealing because I want individual artists and familiar songs today, while Batman and x give me too little information to judge whether they fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock does not make every rock album equally appealing; the Lynyrd Skynyrd hits collection feels more relevant today than How to Dismantle An Atomic.",
    "An older recording or a greatest-hits title is only part of the appeal: Patsy Cline's collection interests me, but it does not match my current rock preference as closely."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of best-of albums and compilations suggest that a collection of familiar songs is especially appealing, which is why I would choose the Skynyrd compilation over their individual album.",
    "Cheek to Cheek gives me a reason to consider standards, but I would need to know the artist before deciding whether Nice Work If You Can Get it offers that connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices recognize my interest in older rock, but only some capture my stronger preference today for familiar songs gathered in hits collections."
